IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p2-constitution`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 5: ADMINISTRATION (ss 57 to 69).
-- Sections 60 (offices attached to the State Courts) and 69 (the power to make Rules of Court) are machinery and are inert (reason 2 of the coverage table).
-- Where a sentence forbids something and names no bearer ("must not be delivered", "must not be included"), no regulative rule is derived: that would invent an actor (fork F-PASSIVE).

§ `Section 57 -- the Registry of the State Courts`

-- src:1949 | 57.—(1) The Registry of the State Courts is to be open on every day
-- src:1950 | of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.
@ref s 57(1) (src:1949-1950)
GIVEN day IS A `Kind of day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(1) the Registry of the State Courts is to be open on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER day
    WHEN `Ordinary day` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be open on every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays" (a duty lifted by an exception: the requirement does not apply)
    WHEN Saturday THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN Sunday THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Public holiday` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- "every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays": a day in a vacation authorised under section 61 is not excepted, so the Registry is to be open (fork F-VACATION)
    WHEN `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:1954 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the registrar may lawfully sit or carry
-- src:1955 | out the business of the Registry on a Saturday, Sunday or public
-- src:1956 | holiday if —
-- src:1958 | (a) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the
-- src:1959 | concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed the
-- src:1960 | registrar to do so on that day; or
-- src:1962 | (b) in the opinion of the registrar, the business to be
-- src:1963 | despatched is extremely urgent.
@ref s 57(2)(a) and (b) (src:1954-1963)
GIVEN day IS A `Kind of day`
      `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed the registrar to do so on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the registrar the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday"
        IF day EQUALS `Ordinary day` OR day EQUALS `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed the registrar to do so on that day` OR `in the opinion of the registrar the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday if — (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1970 | (3) The office hours of the Registry are such times as the Presiding
-- src:1971 | Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice,
-- src:1972 | may from time to time direct.
@ref s 57(3) (src:1970-1972)
GIVEN `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed that the time is within the office hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(3) the time is within the office hours of the Registry` MEANS
    IF `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed that the time is within the office hours`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the office hours "are such times as the Presiding Judge ... may from time to time direct"; the directions are not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 58 to 61 -- sittings, distribution of business, vacations`

-- src:1978 | 58. At any sitting of a District Court or a Magistrate’s Court both
-- src:1979 | civil and criminal proceedings may be tried.
@ref s 58 (src:1978-1979)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58 both civil and criminal proceedings may be tried at the sitting of the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "any sitting of a District Court or a Magistrate’s Court"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1983 | 59. The distribution of business in the State Courts is to be made in
-- src:1984 | accordance with the directions, which may be of a general or a
-- src:1985 | particular nature, that may be given by the Presiding Judge of the
-- src:1986 | State Courts, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice.
@ref s 59 (src:1983-1986)
GIVEN `the distribution of business accords with the directions of the Presiding Judge of the State Courts given with the concurrence of the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59 the distribution of business in the State Courts has been made in accordance with the directions as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the distribution of business accords with the directions of the Presiding Judge of the State Courts given with the concurrence of the Chief Justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to be made in accordance with the directions" is a bare "is to be" (QB); the Act does not say here what follows when it is not
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2007 | 61. The Chief Justice may authorise vacations for District Courts
-- src:2008 | and Magistrates’ Courts in the exercise of their civil jurisdiction not
-- src:2009 | exceeding 15 days in any calendar year.
@ref s 61 (src:2007-2009)
GIVEN `the vacations are for the exercise of civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of vacation authorised in the calendar year, counting these, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61 the Chief Justice may authorise the vacations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of vacations "in the exercise of their civil jurisdiction"
        IF NOT (`the vacations are for the exercise of civil jurisdiction`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the days of vacation authorised in the calendar year, counting these, in days` AT MOST 15 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not exceeding 15 days in any calendar year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 62 -- the list of touts`

-- src:2013 | 62.—(1) The Presiding Judge of the State Courts may —
-- src:2015 | (a) frame and publish a list of persons proved to his or her
-- src:2016 | satisfaction, by evidence of general repute or otherwise, to
-- src:2017 | act as touts or unauthorised advisers to suitors or other
-- src:2018 | persons; and
-- src:2023 | (b) alter and amend the list.
@ref s 62(1)(a) and (b) (src:2013-2023)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(1) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may frame, publish, alter and amend the list of touts` MEANS
    IF holder EQUALS `Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "The Presiding Judge of the State Courts may"; it says nothing of any other officer
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 62(1)(a) (src:2013-2023)
GIVEN `the person is proved to the satisfaction of the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, by evidence of general repute or otherwise, to act as a tout or unauthorised adviser to suitors or other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(1)(a) the person may be named in the list of touts` MEANS
    IF `the person is proved to the satisfaction of the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, by evidence of general repute or otherwise, to act as a tout or unauthorised adviser to suitors or other persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the list is "of persons proved to his or her satisfaction"; the satisfaction is the Presiding Judge's (a judgment handed to someone else), and subsection (3) is a further condition
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2027 | (2) The Presiding Judge of the State Courts may, by general or
-- src:2028 | special order, exclude from the precincts of the State Courts any
-- src:2029 | person whose name is included in the list, except that when the person
-- src:2030 | is a party to or a witness in any proceedings in a State Court, then he
-- src:2031 | or she is allowed to remain for such time as is necessary.
@ref s 62(2) (src:2027-2031)
GIVEN `the person's name is included in the list of touts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may exclude the person from the precincts of the State Courts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any person whose name is included in the list"
        IF NOT (`the person's name is included in the list of touts`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except that when the person is a party to or a witness in any proceedings in a State Court, then he or she is allowed to remain for such time as is necessary"; the exception lifts the power for that time and a lifted power grants nothing (QA)
        IF `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in a State Court` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 62(2) (src:2027-2031)
GIVEN `the person's name is included in the list of touts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(2) the person is allowed to remain in the precincts of the State Courts for such time as is necessary` MEANS
    IF `the person's name is included in the list of touts` AND `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in a State Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the person who is allowed to remain is the one named in the list who is "a party to or a witness in any proceedings in a State Court"; for anyone else the subsection says nothing about staying
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2035 | (3) A person’s name must not be included in the list until the person
-- src:2036 | has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against such
-- src:2037 | inclusion.
@ref s 62(3) (src:2035-2037)
GIVEN `the person has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against the inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(3) the person's name may be included in the list of touts` MEANS
    IF `the person has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against the inclusion`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not be included in the list until the person has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard"; once heard, the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA); the grant is subsection (1)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person’s name must not be included in the list until the person has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against such inclusion" (the text names no bearer, so no regulative rule is derived: F-PASSIVE)
         JUST FALSE

-- src:2039 | (4) An appeal lies to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General
-- src:2040 | Division of the High Court from an order made by the Presiding
-- src:2041 | Judge of the State Courts to include a person’s name in the list.
@ref s 62(4) (src:2039-2041)
GIVEN `it is an order made by the Presiding Judge of the State Courts to include a person's name in the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(4) an appeal lies to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division of the High Court` MEANS
    IF `it is an order made by the Presiding Judge of the State Courts to include a person's name in the list`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal lies "from an order made by the Presiding Judge ... to include a person’s name in the list"; an order of another kind is not mentioned
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2045 | (5) The decision of the Judge is final.
@ref s 62(5) (src:2045)
GIVEN `it is the decision of the Judge on an appeal under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(5) the decision of the Judge is final` MEANS
    IF `it is the decision of the Judge on an appeal under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "The decision of the Judge" under subsection (4)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2049 | (6) A copy of the list is to be kept hung up in the office or offices of
-- src:2050 | the State Courts and must be published in the Gazette.
@ref s 62(6) (src:2049-2050)
GIVEN `a copy of the list is kept hung up in the office or offices of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(6) a copy of the list is kept hung up and the list has been published in the Gazette as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the list is kept hung up in the office or offices of the State Courts` AND `the list has been published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to be kept hung up ... and must be published in the Gazette" is a bare "is to" and "must" (QB); the Act does not say here what follows when it is not
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2054 | (7) A person whose name appears in the list of touts under
-- src:2055 | section 73 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, or the list of
-- src:2056 | touts under section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014, is deemed to be
-- src:2057 | included in the list under this section, and vice versa.
@ref s 62(7) (src:2054-2057)
GIVEN `the person's name appears in the list of touts under section 73 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 or section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under this section` MEANS
    IF `the person's name appears in the list of touts under section 73 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 or section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "A person whose name appears in the list of touts under" those two sections; other lists are not mentioned
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 62(7) (and vice versa) (src:2054-2057)
GIVEN `the person's name appears in the list under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under section 73 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 or section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014` MEANS
    IF `the person's name appears in the list under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and vice versa" runs the deeming the other way for a person named in the list under this section
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 63 -- impounding documents`

-- src:2063 | 63.—(1) A State Court may order any document produced before it
-- src:2064 | in any proceedings to be impounded.
@ref s 63(1) (src:2063-2064)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
      `the document was produced before the court in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) a State Court may order the document to be impounded` MEANS
    IF `s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` court EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the document was produced before the court in proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "A State Court" over "any document produced before it in any proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2068 | (2) The document which has been impounded must not be delivered
-- src:2069 | out of the custody of the court or inspected except on an order signed
-- src:2070 | by a judicial officer.
@ref s 63(2) (src:2068-2070)
GIVEN `the document has been impounded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an order signed by a judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(2) the impounded document may be delivered out of the custody of the court or inspected` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "The document which has been impounded"
        IF NOT (`the document has been impounded`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except on an order signed by a judicial officer"; with the order the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
        IF `there is an order signed by a judicial officer` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be delivered out of the custody of the court or inspected except on an order signed by a judicial officer" (the text names no bearer, so no regulative rule is derived: F-PASSIVE)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2072 | (3) The court that impounded the document may direct the
-- src:2073 | document to be sent to the Attorney-General, the Commissioner of
-- src:2074 | Stamp Duties or any other officer of the Government.
@ref s 63(3) (src:2072-2074)
GIVEN `the court is the court that impounded the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(3) the court may direct the document to be sent to the Attorney-General, the Commissioner of Stamp Duties or any other officer of the Government` MEANS
    IF `the court is the court that impounded the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "The court that impounded the document"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 64 to 66 -- judicial officers and officers of the State Courts`

-- src:2081 | 64.—(1) Except with the approval of the Chief Justice, a judicial
-- src:2082 | officer —
-- src:2084 | (a) shall not be capable of —
-- src:2086 | (i) accepting or taking any other office of emolument; or
-- src:2088 | (ii) carrying on any business either directly or indirectly;
-- src:2089 | and
@ref s 64(1)(a) (src:2081-2089)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1)(a) the judicial officer is capable of accepting or taking another office of emolument or carrying on a business` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has approved`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except with the approval of the Chief Justice"; with approval the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a judicial officer shall not be capable of — (i) accepting or taking any other office of emolument; or (ii) carrying on any business either directly or indirectly"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:2081 | 64.—(1) Except with the approval of the Chief Justice, a judicial
-- src:2082 | officer —
-- src:2091 | (b) must not accept any fees of office, perquisites, emoluments
-- src:2092 | or advantages, other than the judicial officer’s salary and
-- src:2093 | allowances.
@ref s 64(1)(b) (src:2081-2093)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advantage is the judicial officer's salary or allowances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1)(b) the judicial officer may accept the fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than the judicial officer’s salary and allowances" takes them out of the prohibition (QE: a limit on a prohibition, so NOTHING)
        IF `the advantage is the judicial officer's salary or allowances` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except with the approval of the Chief Justice"; with approval the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
        IF `the Chief Justice has approved` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not accept any fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages, other than the judicial officer’s salary and allowances"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 64(1)(b) (src:2081-2093)
-- The prohibition in s 64(1)(b) as a regulative rule: a judicial officer must not accept fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages other than salary and allowances.
-- The Act states no time limit and no consequence, so none is written.
`s 64(1)(b) duty: a judicial officer must not accept fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages` MEANS
    PARTY `A judicial officer`
    SHANT `accept fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages other than salary and allowances`

-- src:2097 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a judicial officer may, with the
-- src:2098 | approval of the Chief Justice —
-- src:2100 | (a) be appointed to any commission of inquiry, committee of
-- src:2101 | inquiry or other judicial, quasi-judicial or administrative
-- src:2102 | tribunal, or hold any office in any institution or society for
-- src:2103 | charitable purposes or for the advancement or
-- src:2104 | encouragement of art, science, education or other
-- src:2105 | knowledge; and
@ref s 64(2)(a) (src:2097-2105)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an appointment to a commission of inquiry, committee of inquiry or other judicial, quasi-judicial or administrative tribunal, or an office in an institution or society for charitable purposes or for the advancement or encouragement of art, science, education or other knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2)(a) the judicial officer may be appointed to the body or hold the office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over appointments and offices of the kinds listed in paragraph (a), "Without limiting subsection (1)"
        IF NOT (`it is an appointment to a commission of inquiry, committee of inquiry or other judicial, quasi-judicial or administrative tribunal, or an office in an institution or society for charitable purposes or for the advancement or encouragement of art, science, education or other knowledge`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice has approved` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a judicial officer may, with the approval of the Chief Justice — (a) be appointed ..." (a failed condition of approval is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2097 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a judicial officer may, with the
-- src:2098 | approval of the Chief Justice —
-- src:2107 | (b) receive an allowance or other honorarium in respect of that
-- src:2108 | appointment or office.
@ref s 64(2)(b) (src:2097-2108)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an allowance or other honorarium in respect of an appointment or office mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2)(b) the judicial officer may receive the allowance or other honorarium` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "an allowance or other honorarium in respect of that appointment or office"
        IF NOT (`it is an allowance or other honorarium in respect of an appointment or office mentioned in paragraph (a)`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice has approved` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a judicial officer may, with the approval of the Chief Justice — ... (b) receive an allowance or other honorarium" (a failed condition of approval is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2114 | 65. A judicial officer must not, except with the approval of the
-- src:2115 | Chief Justice and with the consent of the parties, investigate, try or
-- src:2116 | commit for trial any proceedings to which the judicial officer is a
-- src:2117 | party or in which the judicial officer is personally interested.
@ref s 65 (src:2114-2117)
GIVEN `the judicial officer is a party to the proceedings or personally interested in them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65 the judicial officer may investigate, try or commit for trial the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on proceedings "to which the judicial officer is a party or in which the judicial officer is personally interested"
        IF NOT (`the judicial officer is a party to the proceedings or personally interested in them`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except with the approval of the Chief Justice and with the consent of the parties"; with both the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
        IF `the Chief Justice has approved` AND `the parties have consented` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A judicial officer must not, except with the approval of the Chief Justice and with the consent of the parties, investigate, try or commit for trial any proceedings to which the judicial officer is a party or in which the judicial officer is personally interested"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 65 (src:2114-2117)
-- The prohibition in s 65 as a regulative rule: a judicial officer must not investigate, try or commit for trial a proceeding in which the officer is a party or personally interested (the exception for approval and consent is carried by the decision function above).
`s 65 duty: a judicial officer must not investigate, try or commit for trial a proceeding in which the officer is a party or personally interested` MEANS
    PARTY `A judicial officer`
    SHANT `investigate, try or commit for trial a proceeding in which the judicial officer is a party or personally interested`

-- src:2121 | 66. An officer of the State Courts having any duty to perform in
-- src:2122 | connection with the sale of any property under any written law must
-- src:2123 | not, directly or indirectly, purchase or bid for the property.
@ref s 66 (src:2121-2123)
GIVEN `the officer of the State Courts has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66 the officer may purchase or bid for the property` MEANS
    IF `the officer of the State Courts has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An officer of the State Courts having any duty to perform in connection with the sale of any property under any written law must not, directly or indirectly, purchase or bid for the property"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is on an officer "having any duty to perform in connection with the sale"; for another officer it says nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 66 (src:2121-2123)
-- The prohibition in s 66 as a regulative rule.
`s 66 duty: an officer of the State Courts having a duty in connection with a sale must not purchase or bid for the property` MEANS
    PARTY `An officer of a State Court`
    SHANT `purchase or bid for property sold in connection with a duty of the officer`

§ `Sections 67 and 68 -- misconduct of officers; protection from suit`

-- src:2132 | 67.—(1) Without affecting any written law and rules governing the
-- src:2133 | conduct and discipline of public officers, if any officer of a State
-- src:2134 | Court is charged —
-- src:2136 | (a) with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of
-- src:2137 | the process of the court; or
-- src:2139 | (b) with not duly paying or accounting for any money levied
-- src:2140 | by him or her under the authority of this Act or Rules of
-- src:2141 | Court,
-- src:2143 | it is lawful for a District Judge nominated by the Presiding Judge of
-- src:2144 | the State Courts to inquire into the matter in a summary manner.
@ref s 67(1)(a) and (b) (src:2132-2144)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has nominated the District Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of a State Court is charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer of a State Court is charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied by the officer under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1) it is lawful for the District Judge to inquire into the matter in a summary manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of "a District Judge nominated by the Presiding Judge of the State Courts"
        IF NOT (holder EQUALS `District Judge` AND `the Presiding Judge of the State Courts has nominated the District Judge`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the officer of a State Court is charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the court` OR `the officer of a State Court is charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied by the officer under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if any officer of a State Court is charged — (a) ...; or (b) ..., it is lawful for a District Judge ... to inquire" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2148 | (2) For the purpose of any such inquiry, the District Judge may
-- src:2149 | summon and enforce the attendance of all necessary parties in the like
-- src:2150 | manner as the attendance of witnesses in any case may be enforced.
@ref s 67(2) (src:2148-2150)
GIVEN `it is an inquiry under section 67` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(2) the District Judge may summon and enforce the attendance of all necessary parties` MEANS
    IF `it is an inquiry under section 67`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of any such inquiry"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2152 | (3) On any such inquiry, the District Judge may make such order as
-- src:2153 | he or she thinks just for the repayment of the money extorted or the
-- src:2154 | due payment of the money levied, and for the payment of damages
-- src:2155 | and costs, and also, if he or she thinks fit, may impose such fine upon
-- src:2156 | the officer, not exceeding $100 for each offence, as appears to the
-- src:2157 | District Judge to be adequate.
@ref s 67(3) (src:2152-2157)
GIVEN `it is an inquiry under section 67` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Judge thinks it just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(3) the District Judge may order repayment of the money extorted or payment of the money levied, damages and costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On any such inquiry"
        IF NOT (`it is an inquiry under section 67`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the District Judge thinks it just` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such order as he or she thinks just"; the judgment is the District Judge's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 67(3) (src:2152-2157)
GIVEN `it is an inquiry under section 67` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Judge thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars for each offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(3) the District Judge may impose the fine upon the officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On any such inquiry"
        IF NOT (`it is an inquiry under section 67`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such fine upon the officer, not exceeding $100 for each offence"
        IF `the fine in dollars for each offence` GREATER THAN 100 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the District Judge thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he or she thinks fit"; the judgment is the District Judge's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2159 | (4) If it is found by a District Judge that any officer, while employed
-- src:2160 | in carrying out his or her duties under this Act or Rules of Court or in
-- src:2161 | exercising any of the powers thereof, has wilfully and corruptly
-- src:2162 | exacted or accepted any fee or reward, other than any fees that are for
-- src:2163 | the time being allowed under this Act or Rules of Court, that officer
-- src:2164 | shall, in addition to being liable for damages under subsection (3), be
-- src:2165 | incapable of being an officer of the State Courts.
@ref s 67(4) (src:2159-2165)
GIVEN `a District Judge has found that the officer, while employed in carrying out duties under this Act or Rules of Court or in exercising powers under them, wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted a fee or reward other than a fee for the time being allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(4) the officer is incapable of being an officer of the State Courts` MEANS
    IF `a District Judge has found that the officer, while employed in carrying out duties under this Act or Rules of Court or in exercising powers under them, wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted a fee or reward other than a fee for the time being allowed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it is found by a District Judge that any officer ... has wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted any fee or reward ..., that officer shall ... be incapable of being an officer of the State Courts" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

