GIVEN `it is an order made by the District Judge under section 67` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(5) an appeal lies to the Chief Justice` MEANS
    IF `it is an order made by the District Judge under section 67`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal lies "from an order made by the District Judge under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2172 | (6) The decision of the Chief Justice is final.
